{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-86791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $16{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+4x+64y+44=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-86791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+4x+64y+44 & =0 \\\\ 16{y}^{2}+64y-{x}^{2}+4x & =-44 \\\\ 16[{y}^{2}+4y]-[{x}^{2}-4x] & =-44 \\\\ 16[(y+2)^{2}-4]-[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =-44 \\\\ 16(y+2)^{2}-64-(x-2)^{2}+4 & =-44 \\\\ 16(y+2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =-44+64-4 \\\\ 16(y+2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{16(y+2)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{16}{16} \\\\ (y+2)^{2}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(2,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{1}=1,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-86791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db2001aa0f2e3934ad8e3f6f40db440f45dea1516e025201c279f7821d830cf1"} {"question" "q-86791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-86791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm 4(x-2)"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x+2)"] ["math" "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x-2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm 2(x+2)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm 4(x+2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-86791" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y+2=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x-2)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola \n${y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}-4y+50x-46=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}-4y+50x-46 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y-25{x}^{2}+50x-46 & =0 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-4y]-25[{x}^{2}-2x]-46 & =0 \\\\ [(y-2)^{2}-4]-25[(x-1)^{2}-1]-46 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-25(x-1)^{2}+25-46 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-25(x-1)^{2} & =46+4-25 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-25(x-1)^{2} & =25 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25}-(x-1)^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe asymptotes of a vertical hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(1,2),\\,a=\\sqrt{25}=5,\\,b=\\sqrt{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\ny-2=\\pm 5(x-1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db2001aa0f2e3934ad8e3f6f40db440f45dea1516e025201c279f7821d830cf1"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y+2=\\pm 2(x+1)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm 5(x+1)"] ["math" "y-1=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}(x-1)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm 5(x-1)"] ["math" "y-2=\\pm \\frac{1}{5}(x-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-165483" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y-2=\\pm 5(x-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{27}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(-3,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}})(x-(-3)) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{2}{3}(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325365" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db2001aa0f2e3934ad8e3f6f40db440f45dea1516e025201c279f7821d830cf1"} {"question" "q-325365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325365" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}(x+3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}=1.$\n\n$y\\,\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$=\\pm $\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(0,-4),\\,a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2},\\,b=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-4) & =\\pm (\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3\\sqrt{2}})(x-0) \\\\ y+4 & =\\pm \\,\\frac{2}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db2001aa0f2e3934ad8e3f6f40db440f45dea1516e025201c279f7821d830cf1"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325369" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-150x-8y+121=0.$\n\n$y\\,\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$=\\pm $\n{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}-150x-8y+121 & =0 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}-6x)-4({y}^{2}+2y)+121 & =0 \\\\ 25\\,[(x-3)^{2}-9]-4\\,[(y+1)^{2}-1]+121 & =0 \\\\ 25(x-3)^{2}-225-4(y+1)^{2}+4+121 & =0 \\\\ 25(x-3)^{2}-4(y+1)^{2} & =100 \\\\ \\frac{25(x-3)^{2}}{100}-\\frac{4(y+1)^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus it is a horizontal hyperbola\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nso the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nHere,\n\n$$\n(h,k)=(3,-1),\\,a=\\sqrt{4}=2,\\,b=\\sqrt{25}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-1) & =\\pm (\\frac{5}{2})(x-3) \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm \\,\\frac{5}{2}(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "db2001aa0f2e3934ad8e3f6f40db440f45dea1516e025201c279f7821d830cf1"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066507/state.json" "file_sha256" "24e19c2a9ca91f5221edbbdd3297a8a4ce9058a6b92705cad809d9d4e5b0d984"} {"question" "q-325434" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}(x-3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/